1
00:00:01,248 --> 00:00:08,620
Welcome to the Asia capitals, episode five of seven. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09,275 --> 00:00:17,588
Seven capitals of the Gulf and the Arabian Peninsula: the bay cities of the
north and the inland capitals of the centre and the south.

3
00:00:18,245 --> 00:00:20,463
Let's bring Kuwait City into view.

4
00:00:25,152 --> 00:00:33,592
Kuwait City stands at the head of the Persian Gulf in the east of Kuwait, on
the bay around which the country grew.

5
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:43,706
Its Kuwait Towers, opened in 1979, have become the country's emblem, and most
of Kuwait's people live in and around it.

6
00:00:44,371 --> 00:00:49,828
Remember Kuwait City as the bay city whose twin towers became the emblem of
the country.

7
00:00:50,523 --> 00:00:53,379
Let's bring Manama into view.

8
00:00:56,635 --> 00:01:06,144
Manama stands on the north coast of Bahrain, an island in the Persian Gulf,
north of Qatar and about 35 kilometres from the Saudi coast.

9
00:01:06,796 --> 00:01:22,237
"Place of rest". Qal'at al-Bahrain, nearby, was the seat of ancient Dilmun and
is a UNESCO site, and the Bahrain World Trade Center has three wind turbines
between its two towers.

10
00:01:22,899 --> 00:01:30,910
Remember Manama as the place of rest beside ancient Dilmun, and the towers
with wind turbines between them.

11
00:01:31,601 --> 00:01:33,563
Let's bring Doha into view.

12
00:01:38,851 --> 00:01:45,411
Doha stands on the east coast of the Qatar peninsula, on the bay facing the
Persian Gulf.

13
00:01:46,071 --> 00:01:54,337
A village of pearl divers that grew rich on oil and gas, its Museum of Islamic
Art was designed by I. M. Pei.

14
00:01:54,996 --> 00:02:02,032
Remember Doha as the pearl divers' village that grew rich, with I. M. Pei's
museum on the bay.

15
00:02:02,718 --> 00:02:05,400
Let's bring Abu Dhabi into view.

16
00:02:09,384 --> 00:02:17,360
Abu Dhabi stands on an island off the coast of the Persian Gulf, in the west
of the United Arab Emirates, north of Dubai.

17
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:28,761
"Father of the gazelle". The Louvre Abu Dhabi opened in 2017 under a dome of
latticed steel, and the Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque has one of the largest
carpets in the world.

18
00:02:29,419 --> 00:02:36,710
Remember Abu Dhabi as the father of the gazelle, with the Louvre under its
lattice dome by the gulf.

19
00:02:37,464 --> 00:02:40,018
Let's bring Riyadh into view.

20
00:02:48,546 --> 00:02:55,535
Riyadh stands in the centre of the Arabian Peninsula, in the Najd highlands,
in the middle of Saudi Arabia.

21
00:02:56,199 --> 00:03:06,567
"The gardens", for the oases where it grew. The Masmak fortress, taken by Ibn
Saud in 1902, marks the start of the modern kingdom.

22
00:03:07,219 --> 00:03:15,102
Remember Riyadh as the gardens of the Najd oases, where the Masmak fortress
marks the start of the kingdom.

23
00:03:15,889 --> 00:03:17,758
Let's bring Muscat into view.

24
00:03:27,084 --> 00:03:36,256
Muscat stands on the coast of Oman, at the foot of the mountains that block
the interior, on the Gulf of Oman.

25
00:03:36,907 --> 00:03:48,331
Two Portuguese forts of the 16th century, Jalali and Mirani, guard its old
harbour, and its Royal Opera House, opened in 2011, was the first in the Gulf.

26
00:03:48,989 --> 00:03:55,595
Remember Muscat as the harbour guarded by two Portuguese forts, and the Gulf's
first opera house.

27
00:03:56,321 --> 00:03:58,062
Let's bring Sanaa into view.

28
00:04:04,901 --> 00:04:15,176
Sanaa stands on the highland plateau of northern Yemen, about 2,250 metres
above the Red Sea coast.

29
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:23,513
By tradition it was founded by Shem, a son of Noah, and its Great Mosque is
one of the oldest in the Islamic world.

30
00:04:24,170 --> 00:04:32,959
Remember Sanaa as the high plateau capital founded by tradition by a son of
Noah, with one of Islam's oldest great mosques.

31
00:04:37,817 --> 00:04:53,585
Kuwait City, Manama and Doha line the Gulf's northern shore, with Abu Dhabi
further west. Riyadh stands inland in the Najd highlands, Muscat on the coast
of Oman, and Sanaa high on the Yemeni plateau.

32
00:04:54,252 --> 00:05:11,028
Remember the twin towers of the emblem, the place of rest beside ancient
Dilmun, the pearl divers who grew rich, the father of the gazelle, the gardens
of the oases, the harbour of two Portuguese forts, and the city founded by a
son of Noah.
